7ru3|v|To arrange and present the reasons for or against; to examine or discuss by arguments; to debate or discuss; as, I reasoned the matter with my friend. ; To support with reasons, as a request. ; To persuade by reasoning or argument; as, to reason one into a belief; to reason one out of his plan. ; To overcome or conquer by adducing reasons; -- with down; as, to reason down a passion. ; To find by logical processes; to explain or justify by reason or argument; -- usually with out; as, to reason out the causes of the librations of the moon.	s:7h1m,66,5~7h1m,66,5
