7urg|v|The compass of a voice or instrument; a specified portion of the compass of a voice, or a series of vocal tones of a given compass; as, the upper, middle, or lower register; the soprano register; the tenor register. ; A stop or set of pipes in an organ. ; To enroll one's name in a register. ; To correspond in relative position; as, two pages, columns, etc. , register when the corresponding parts fall in the same line, or when line falls exactly upon line in reverse pages, or (as in chromatic printing) where the various colors of the design are printed consecutively, and perfect adjustment of parts is necessary.	o:4qxn,95,12;13bi,92,5;4tz7,82,4;9knr,74,7;3kx6,66,38;7h5o,65,2;9kt0,65,7;13y7,63,2;13y4,62,13;493y,61,2;oo5,60,2;8y34,60,17;8p8x,57,8;5zge,56,3;9yj9,53,5~319b,5,576;186o,41,223;31h8,3,199;13xk,31,196;5al8,39,186;3yja,25,128;1ocy,22,128;8idn,0,114;859d,16,100;1keh,13,89;5akw,7,69;2jtx,2,52;13y3,31,46;2l3p,6,40;3kx6,66,38	s:8jfi,93,6;81cy,55,1;78hw,54,7;25jb,41,4;6krv,41,12;6c7q,39,1;2s0t,38,4;14c6,33,1;9nam,31,1;1895,25,13;2df9,22,14;4mc,21,12;5f8a,19,1;4z54,15,2;abrw,13,2~a75m,7,649;3byt,0,57;1keh,3,44;1sxh,11,14;2df9,22,14;1895,25,13;6krv,41,12;4mc,21,12;6juo,5,11;7dik,1,9;1pv3,11,8;78hw,54,7;97ji,5,7;8jfi,93,6;2s0t,38,4	d:28i4,42,11;2gcw,30,5;1scs,29,15;aejw,25,11;rua,24,70;6kuz,19,46;oaz,19,666;1r1w,19,25;55fh,17,8;7gcp,16,83;2puv,16,211;5jox,15,417;eay,12,3;9858,10,169;91qd,9,19~oaz,19,666;5jox,15,417;2puv,16,211;33sw,6,177;9858,10,169;7gcp,16,83;rua,24,70;6kuz,19,46;1r1w,19,25;91qd,9,19;1scs,29,15;aejw,25,11;28i4,42,11;55fh,17,8;2gcw,30,5	D:13y7,53,1;9xr8,49,2;7shd,43,3;64zf,40,3;1tfk,38,4;8smv,33,2;7sem,19,3;e5y,16,3;7s8i,12,76;6nl6,11,3;66jk,9,8;4k03,7,2~7s8i,12,76;66jk,9,8;1tfk,38,4;7shd,43,3;6nl6,11,3;64zf,40,3;7sem,19,3;e5y,16,3;9xr8,49,2;8smv,33,2;4k03,7,2;13y7,53,1
