7vp0|n|A supply of anything arranged beforehand for affording relief from time to time, or at successive stages; provision for successive relief. ; A supply of horses placced at stations to be in readiness to relieve others, so that a trveler may proceed without delay. ; A supply of hunting dogs or horses kept in readiness at certain places to relive the tired dogs or horses, and to continue the pursuit of the game if it comes that way. ; A number of men who relieve others in carrying on some work. ; In various forms of telegraphic apparatus, a magnet which receives the circuit current, and is caused by it to bring into into action the power of a local battery for performing the work of making the record; also, a similar device by which the current in one circuit is made to open or close another circuit in which a current is passing.	a:7n0e,124,31;8uz2,117,38;9k3u,111,10;2t3l,108,199;mzr,105,11;9k3q,103,10;yap,101,63;889u,101,26;6p64,94,4;u6l,93,3;hov,92,9;3lmu,91,13;44sg,91,5;9hx0,90,37;3c4e,84,28~6nwu,28,1314;5okf,67,801;8p3m,5,272;913b,65,257;8s1h,11,254;a800,1,222;8pm3,4,220;7amb,57,220;218w,1,211;2t3l,108,199;odh,80,198;1662,37,179;4kkj,17,156;7jn2,45,137;34dz,12,128	v:u6l,117,16;54of,116,1067;6p6e,105,13;aikz,77,15;6p64,74,1;2wd9,74,1;889u,70,3;a2ww,69,2;4ksi,68,4;2wdd,68,13;8i81,67,5;7tre,67,93;1fmc,65,4;8uz2,64,1;iz3,60,5~54of,116,1067;7q63,46,149;1u32,40,140;1l35,4,93;7tre,67,93;9bfs,21,75;333o,1,67;2nm0,2,52;8h0g,53,48;1u4p,30,38;80zt,34,22;3ds,34,17;u6l,117,16;aikz,77,15;6ogn,32,14	V:2wd9,104,8;1j0m,92,4;1fmc,88,20;2wd7,87,19;1jdo,79,3;2wdh,78,7;2wde,75,50;1n33,73,212;16oq,72,6;3sf,70,14;3sh,65,4;2hpe,61,2;3ckf,61,4;2wdi,57,3;1fmg,57,1~1t1u,50,323;68ew,13,282;9bfm,48,272;9bfs,39,265;1n33,73,212;1rz5,17,207;7q63,50,189;9wrz,27,189;7yfa,15,168;1u32,42,163;7y7e,51,160;3p6h,7,154;a7cv,2,130;2nwf,39,101;2nog,35,101	n:73ru,117,17;2mmm,116,527;8uz2,115,34;8woq,109,397;2mp8,107,66;48mv,106,6;u6l,103,6;6p6t,102,3;8ymv,98,107;73oe,96,6;54of,94,237;1er5,93,59;50xl,9